## KOT slip format (match the real THE BOSS sample)

File: `src/server/hardware/escpos.ts`

- Station title large/centered (`BAR` / `KITCHEN`), then `Restaurant KOT`
- Fields: `KOT No.`, `Table No.`, `Date` (`17 Nov 2026  18:25:07`), `Stward` (same spelling as sample)
- Centered bold underline order banner, then `Original Copy` / `Reprint Copy`:
  - **NEW ORDER** — first KOT on that table session (table’s first punch)
  - **RUNNING ORDER** — table already running (later KOTs / additions / cancel slips)
- Table: `Item Name|Qty` with a vertical bar; more items = longer slip (feed + cut, no fixed page)
- **Remark** prints under the item table after a rule line (sample text under AAA was the Remark field, not a second item)
- Print KOT (F5) sends `{ remark }` with `/api/orders/:id/send-kot`
- Match **native IBS** KOT (bottom slip / 18:33 sample): Font A, **48 cols**, BAR **heavy** (bold + double-strike) + double-width/height (`ESC ! 0x30`), tight meta block, centered NEW ORDER or RUNNING ORDER with thick underline then Original/Reprint Copy, **bold** `Item Name|Qty` header, solid rules (not dashed `-`), darker body/remark
- ESC/POS Font A is fixed-pitch (TM-T82 raw TCP) — match native weight/spacing/alignment; do not switch to Windows GDI
- **Do not** leave `GS L` / `GS W` margins set — they stick on the TM-T82 and can clip **Qty** on later IBS Windows prints. Always `ESC @` at start and after cut.
- TM-T82 ESC/POS over TCP 9100

